 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Why did a gray horse beat Peter Cooper's steam train?",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 2.54
  },
  {
   "text": "His engine, Tom Thumb, is the size of a cart. The whole railroad rides on it.",
   "s": 2.84,
   "e": 6.999
  },
  {
   "text": "Stagecoach men laugh at it, so they bring their fastest horse and dare him to race.",
   "s": 7.199,
   "e": 11.482
  },
  {
   "text": "Two tracks, side by side, thirteen miles to Baltimore.",
   "s": 11.682,
   "e": 14.461
  },
  {
   "text": "The horse bolts ahead, while Tom Thumb is still coughing and spitting steam.",
   "s": 14.661,
   "e": 18.149
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the little engine roars, catches the horse, and passes him!",
   "s": 18.349,
   "e": 21.244
  },
  {
   "text": "Passengers cheer and wave their hats at the poor horse.",
   "s": 21.444,
   "e": 23.925
  },
  {
   "text": "But then a belt snaps off the fan, and the fire starts to die!",
   "s": 24.125,
   "e": 26.798
  },
  {
   "text": "Cooper scrambles to fix it, but the engine wheezes down to a crawl.",
   "s": 26.998,
   "e": 30.275
  },
  {
   "text": "The horse trots right past him and wins.",
   "s": 30.675,
   "e": 32.475
  },
  {
   "text": "So why did the railroad pick the loser?",
   "s": 32.675,
   "e": 34.319
  },
  {
   "text": "Because for one whole minute, everyone saw a machine outrun a horse.",
   "s": 34.619,
   "e": 37.889
  },
  {
   "text": "Within a year, they bought steam engines, and the horses went home.",
   "s": 38.09,
   "e": 40.96
  },
  {
   "text": "So how does a horse win the race, and still lose?",
   "s": 41.16,
   "e": 43.388
  }
 ],
